From 4ef57bb75c9612ce81fdb7967ab56c463303ad05 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daryl Denson <9751141+denson9874@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 07:46:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] config: keep the stock 60 fps default frame rate for games

Evolution X carries "config: Disable default frame rate limit for
games" (HeCheng Yu, 74a5857d76c5), which sets
debug.graphics.game_default_frame_rate.disabled=true. It was added
because Android 15 holds games at 60 fps unless the developer option
"Disable default frame rate for games" is turned on by hand, and the
prop turns that option on for everyone. Upstream LineageOS doesn't set
it, and neither does stock Pixel firmware.

With the prop set, GameManagerService never passes
ro.surface_flinger.game_default_frame_rate_override (60, from AOSP's
base_system.mk) on to SurfaceFlinger. Games that don't pick a frame
rate themselves then run up to the panel's peak refresh rate, with the
heat and battery drain that comes with it.

Drop the prop so games start at 60 fps again, as on stock. Games that
set their own frame rate still get it, and the developer option still
lifts the limit until the next reboot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 config/common.mk | 4 ----
 1 file changed, 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/config/common.mk b/config/common.mk
index 6c855c88..c5974b1f 100644
--- a/config/common.mk
+++ b/config/common.mk
@@ -228,10 +228,6 @@ PRODUCT_COPY_FILES += \
 PRODUCT_PACKAGES += \
     SimpleSettingsConfig
 
-# Disable default frame rate limit for games
-PRODUCT_PRODUCT_PROPERTIES += \
-    debug.graphics.game_default_frame_rate.disabled=true
-
 # Disable RescueParty due to high risk of data loss
 PRODUCT_PRODUCT_PROPERTIES += \
     persist.sys.disable_rescue=true
